# python
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# texture review renders -- regenerate with tools/texview.py, never commit
# (except the worked example in docs/img, which is deliberately tracked)
*_view.png

# gradle/MDG run artifacts
run/
!run/.gitkeep

# Datagen's hash cache. NOT committed, and that is a guard rather than tidiness.
# HashCache skips writing a file whose newly-generated hash matches the cached one
# WITHOUT looking at the file on disk -- so a hand-edited generated file that gets
# committed survives every later `runServerData`, and the staleness gate reports clean.
# See docs/LESSONS.md #37. CI deletes this directory before regenerating; keeping it out
# of the repository is what makes that the only possible state.
src/generated/resources/.cache/
